  "asr_text": "Are people who earn more always more hardworking? When people talk about income and personality, they often start looking for traits that successful people share. But this time, let's ask the high earner next door to step off stage for a moment. The person in the spotlight is none other than you. The research team brought together and analyzed data from 11 studies that followed the same people. The participants were working people who reported their personality and income from work. Their personality and income were each surveyed at least three times. So this was not a single snapshot, but a series of photos showing changes over time. The direction of the camera matters here. The researchers separated the differences between people, that person is more hardworking than me and also earns more, from changes within the same person, how did my personality change after my income changed? They moved from ranking people by yearly income to tracking one person over time. It's a different contest altogether.",
